\\}+2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\cdot t}-3{e}^{1\\cdot t}+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}-3{e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t}+1 \\\\ {e}^{3t}-3{e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534721 17592186045417 true] [17592186434063 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434043 13194139534721 17592186045417 true] [17592186434063 1069 "q-332785" 13194139534721 17592186045417 true] [17592186434063 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534721 17592186045417 true] [17592186434063 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." 13194139534721 17592186045417 true] [17592186434063 1072 #uuid "8dcb1599-ae92-594f-a29c-09dd73cb7136" 13194139534721 17592186045417 true] [17592186434063 1074 "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+3\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+3L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1=3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{3}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1 & =3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-1 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =-\\frac{1}{s-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-2 & =-2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =-2{X}_{1}(s)+2+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =-2(-\\frac{1}{s-3})+2+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =(\\frac{2}{s-3})+(\\frac{2s+3}{s}) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+(2s+3)(s-3)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+(2{s}^{2}-3s-9)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s-9}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s-9}{s(s-1)(s-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s-9}{s(s-1)(s-3)}.\n$$" 13194139534721 17592186045417 true] [17592186434064 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434044 13194139534721 17592186045417 true] [17592186434064 1069 "q-333055" 13194139534721 17592186045417 true] [17592186434064 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534721 17592186045417 true] [17592186434064 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." 13194139534721 17592186045417 true] [17592186434064 1072 #uuid "b4ba1928-c543-554d-8f81-96f348be498a" 13194139534721 17592186045417 true] [17592186434064 1074 "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)-2\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-2L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+5L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1=3{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-4=2{X}_{1}(s)+5{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1 & =3{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-1-\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-(1+\\frac{2}{s}) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-(\\frac{s+2}{s}) \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-4 & =2{X}_{1}(s)+5{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)+4 \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =2(-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)})+4 \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =-\\frac{2(s+2)}{s(s-3)}+4 \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2(s+2)+4s(s-3)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2s-4+4{s}^{2}-12s}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)(s-5)}.\n$$" 13194139534721 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0ee4da26-2e46-5514-8576-64346cfef801" 17592186433969 "answer-0f342f7d-f1a7-517d-9ceb-fa32f8e65